{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDIwL1NvcGhpZSUyMEpvbmVzJTIwJTI4MjAyMCUyOS8","type":"movie","name":"Sophie Jones","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/dxEhkIqjiU619thGFOiVbK1svU9.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/yB4oKA0cZZ8Enj51xPbRLV9HUHS.jpg","description":"Inspired by true experiences of grief, girlhood, and growing up, Jessie Barr’s SOPHIE JONES provides a stirring portrait of a sixteen-year-old. Stunned by the untimely death of her mother and struggling with the myriad challenges of teendom, Sophie (played with striking immediacy by the director’s cousin Jessica Barr) tries everything she can to feel something again, while holding herself together, in this sensitive, acutely realized, and utterly relatable coming-of-age story.\n\nReleased 2 Apr 2021 · United States of America · Language: English · 86 min\nStudio: The Sounding Board\n\nOn your server — Audio: English · Subtitle files: English","releaseInfo":"2020","genres":["Drama","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"5.0","runtime":"86 min","cast":["Jessica Barr","Skyler Verity","Claire Manning","Charlie Jackson","Dave Roberts","Tristan Decker","Sam Kamerman","Chase Offerle"],"director":["Jessie Barr"],"released":"2021-04-02T00:00:00.000Z","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Jessie Barr","character":"Director"},{"name":"Jessica Barr","character":"Sophie Jones","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/aqwtVvvRJ291XiPFhe0rByrS0ci.jpg"},{"name":"Skyler Verity","character":"Kevin","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/6zO8CYK8sK6RB9bZuroz5IHzi8h.jpg"},{"name":"Claire Manning","character":"Claire"},{"name":"Charlie Jackson","character":"Lucy Jones"},{"name":"Dave Roberts","character":"Aaron Jones"},{"name":"Tristan Decker","character":"Riley","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/mO8zVDFCO2FvR9TK7gT0A4aqnqR.jpg"},{"name":"Sam Kamerman","character":"Kate","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/tXgZNfwfTtGjao78d71FGQeHiys.jpg"},{"name":"Chase Offerle","